  "query_preview": "Forecast Discussion...\n\nLooking beyond the period, the flow across North America may revert \nback to a split flow pattern with faster flow remaining along the \nUS/Canadian border and an active subtropical jet with continued \ntroughing out in the western CONUS.  The teleconnection pattern \nlooks to gradually support a slightly negative AO/NAO/PNA pattern \nwith a continued +EPO pattern.  Model tendencies suggest that the AO \nand NAO will likely continue to grow negatively with increasing \ntime.  The PNA looks to remain negative with the +EPO pattern \nholding sway.  Overall, this points to at least normal to slightly \nabove normal temperatures for the first part of December.  However, \nsome transient shots of colder temps can't be ruled out, but \nsustained cold does not look likely through mid-December.  There are \nsome signals showing up that a colder pattern could develop by the \nthird week of December, especially if the AO and NAO can become more \nnegative with time.",
